00:00:05.363 --> 00:00:07.030
JEREMY CONDIT: My
name is Jeremy Condit.

00:00:07.030 --> 00:00:09.620
And I'm an engineering
manager on the BigQuery team.

00:00:09.620 --> 00:00:12.590
Fun fact about BigQuery,
lots of Google Cloud products

00:00:12.590 --> 00:00:16.250
had Big code names like BigStore
for storage and BigCluster

00:00:16.250 --> 00:00:18.290
for compute that all
fell by the wayside

00:00:18.290 --> 00:00:20.240
when those products launched.

00:00:20.240 --> 00:00:22.040
When it came time
to launch BigQuery,

00:00:22.040 --> 00:00:23.300
we considered renaming it.

00:00:23.300 --> 00:00:25.790
But in the end, we decided
that there was no better way

00:00:25.790 --> 00:00:29.320
to describe the unique power of
our product than Big and Query.

00:00:29.320 --> 00:00:31.070
So the name stuck and
the rest is history.

00:00:35.253 --> 00:00:36.920
JORDAN TIGANI: My
name is Jordan Tigani.

00:00:36.920 --> 00:00:40.020
And I'm the director of product
management for Google BigQuery.

00:00:40.020 --> 00:00:42.250
I was one of the founding
engineers on BigQuery

00:00:42.250 --> 00:00:43.053
10 years ago now.

00:00:43.053 --> 00:00:44.720
One of the most
memorable moments for me

00:00:44.720 --> 00:00:48.650
was at Google I/O in 2014
where Felipe Hoffa and I

00:00:48.650 --> 00:00:50.480
used BigQuery on
stage to predict

00:00:50.480 --> 00:00:53.815
the results of the next eight
World Cup matches in Brazil.

00:00:53.815 --> 00:00:55.940
We ended up getting all of
those predictions right.

00:00:55.940 --> 00:00:57.880
And yes, the US did
lose to Belgium.

00:00:57.880 --> 00:00:59.630
But it is possibly the
most stressful time

00:00:59.630 --> 00:01:00.680
in my BigQuery career.

00:01:05.382 --> 00:01:06.590
DAN DELOREY: I'm Dan Delorey.

00:01:06.590 --> 00:01:09.980
I'm a senior engineering
manager on BigQuery.

00:01:09.980 --> 00:01:12.920
I'll actually share my
fun fact about Dremel.

00:01:12.920 --> 00:01:16.700
So for several years, I
was responsible for getting

00:01:16.700 --> 00:01:20.330
internal users, Googlers,
to migrate onto Dremel.

00:01:20.330 --> 00:01:23.640
At that time, we got
to 85% of Googlers

00:01:23.640 --> 00:01:28.890
were using it on a monthly
basis and 75% on a weekly basis.

00:01:28.890 --> 00:01:32.660
And I think that sort of
democratization of data

00:01:32.660 --> 00:01:35.300
is really the benefit
that a tool like BigQuery

00:01:35.300 --> 00:01:37.160
brings to organizations.

00:01:41.112 --> 00:01:42.320
JING JING LONG: Hi, everyone.

00:01:42.320 --> 00:01:45.470
I'm Jing Jing Long, the senior
staff engineer at Google.

00:01:45.470 --> 00:01:48.230
One significant
innovation in BigQuery

00:01:48.230 --> 00:01:52.280
that I'm particularly
proud of is BigQuery ML.

00:01:52.280 --> 00:01:56.810
BigQuery ML enables users
to easily train and use

00:01:56.810 --> 00:02:00.500
machine learning models inside
of BigQuery just using SQL.

00:02:00.500 --> 00:02:03.650
We've seen customers be able
to reduce the amount of time

00:02:03.650 --> 00:02:06.150
and effort it takes to create
a machine learning model

00:02:06.150 --> 00:02:07.700
from months to days.

00:02:11.910 --> 00:02:12.910
MOSHA PASUMANSKY: Hello.

00:02:12.910 --> 00:02:14.250
I'm Mosha Pasumansky.

00:02:14.250 --> 00:02:17.550
And I'm chief BigQuery
officer, meaning

00:02:17.550 --> 00:02:21.060
I get to be involved in
all areas of BigQuery.

00:02:21.060 --> 00:02:23.490
Really, I have the best job.

00:02:23.490 --> 00:02:26.610
If you're getting
started with BigQuery,

00:02:26.610 --> 00:02:30.510
you can go with many different
data warehouse designs.

00:02:30.510 --> 00:02:35.570
You can do classic Kimball
schema or Data Vault or NoSQL

00:02:35.570 --> 00:02:37.920
types of human
structured storage.

00:02:37.920 --> 00:02:41.160
Really, they all
will work very well.

00:02:41.160 --> 00:02:43.720
BigQuery knows how to
deal with all of them.

00:02:43.720 --> 00:02:47.890
So do what makes sense
for your business model.

00:02:47.890 --> 00:02:51.630
I recommend paying attention
to BigQuery's marquee features.

00:02:51.630 --> 00:02:55.230
[INAUDIBLE] Data
Model, [INAUDIBLE],,

00:02:55.230 --> 00:02:58.650
geospatial support,
ML, et cetera,

00:02:58.650 --> 00:03:00.930
because they can significantly
improve your designs.

